"""Verify exact old site text and write Brief 117 proposed additions only."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,re
B=next(p for p in Path(__file__).resolve().parents if (p/'REPO-GUIDE.md').exists())/'docs/production/claude-pm'; A=B/'assets'
site=json.loads((A/'brief117-site-evidence.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
existing=(B/'site-corrections-m8.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8')
water='https://guidelines.nhmrc.gov.au/australian-drinking-water-guidelines/part-5/physical-chemical-characteristics/lead'
insulin='https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK279115/'
death='https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/health/causes-death/causes-death-australia/2024'
rows=[
('chemistry-L04','The ADWG guideline for lead is 0.01','Outdated guideline (the next text is mg L with superscript -1); the example is industrial discharge, so drinking-water compliance is also the wrong regulatory conclusion.','The 2025 Australian drinking-water lead health guideline is 0.005 mg/L. Compare discharge with its applicable licence or receiving-water requirements, not an automatic drinking-water compliance claim.',water),
('chemistry-L04','6.98 / 0.01','Uses the obsolete lead guideline.','6.98/0.005=1396, about 1400, only as a drinking-water comparison. Prefer removing the discharge compliance comparison.',water),
('chemistry-L04','omitting l from the equation','Visible answer button at HTML line 399 says 0.0400 mol/L with this explanation. The example uses a 1.00 cm cell. Omitting l would leave 0.00400 numerically, not 0.0400.','Use a missing-path-length equation as the distractor, or change l and recalculate the example.','Internal arithmetic: 0.480/120=0.00400'),
('chemistry-L08','= 10 000 times the water concentration','The tissue concentration is mg/kg while water is mg/L. The quotient has units L/kg and field data do not isolate water-only uptake.','2.0 mg/kg divided by 0.00020 mg/L is 10000 L/kg, a tissue-to-water field accumulation ratio.','Dimensional analysis of the page values'),
('chemistry-L08','Lead from old plumbing and mercury from coal burning are significant non-industrial sources.','Coal-fired power generation is an industrial mercury source.','Describe plumbing separately from industrial atmospheric mercury deposition.','https://www.dcceew.gov.au/environment/protection/npi/substances/mercury-compounds'),
('biology-L05','Higher light intensity activates the guard cell K⁺ pumps, widening the pores.','The light-activated pump in this account is a proton pump. Potassium uptake follows through channels.','Light activates guard-cell proton pumps; membrane polarisation drives potassium entry, water follows and the pores can open.','https://openstax.org/books/biology-2e/pages/30-5-transport-of-water-and-solutes-in-plants'),
('biology-L06','All five leading causes are non-infectious','The page refers to 2022. COVID-19 was third in 2022.','Name the year; COVID-19 ranked third in 2022, ninth in 2023 and twelfth in 2024 in the ABS release. Use revised data where precise totals are needed.',death),
('biology-L06','Inhaled asbestos fibres scar lung-lining tissue and cause mesothelioma','Conflates lung fibrosis/asbestosis with mesothelioma of the lining.','Asbestos can cause scarring of lung tissue (asbestosis) and cancer of mesothelial linings (mesothelioma).','https://www.cancer.gov/about-cancer/causes-prevention/risk/substances/asbestos/asbestos-fact-sheet'),
('biology-L06','Type 2 diabetes needs both genetic susceptibility (some groups, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, carry a 3 to 4 times higher baseline risk)','Presents a population-rate difference as a fixed genetic baseline; also says both genes and triggers are necessary in every case. Owner cultural review required.','Type 2 diabetes has multiple contributing factors. Differences in population rates do not establish genetic causation. Explain social and environmental determinants, access to food and care, and the effects of inequity. Owner to approve culturally appropriate wording.','https://www.indigenoushpf.gov.au/measures/1-09-diabetes'),
('biology-L06','some ethnic groups (Indigenous Australians, South Asian, Pacific Islander) have higher genetic susceptibility, a baseline that cannot be changed by lifestyle','Infers a fixed genetic cause from population differences. Owner cultural review required.','Do not equate ethnicity or Indigenous status with a fixed genetic baseline. Describe multifactorial risk with the relevant social, environmental and individual factors; owner cultural review before publication.','https://www.indigenoushpf.gov.au/measures/1-09-diabetes'),
('biology-L06','It tracks how fast a disease is spreading through a group.','Incidence also describes non-infectious disease and does not imply transmission.','It tracks the occurrence of new cases in a population over a specified time.','https://www.cdc.gov/csels/dsepd/ss1978/lesson3/section2.html'),
('biology-L07','from the CFTR protein on chromosome 7','The gene is located on chromosome 7, not the protein.','From the CFTR protein, encoded by the CFTR gene on chromosome 7.','https://medlineplus.gov/genetics/gene/cftr/'),
('biology-L07','fewer than 36 repeats is normal, while 36 or more causes disease.','The 27-to-35 intermediate range and reduced penetrance at 36-to-39 are erased.','27 to 35 CAG repeats are intermediate; 36 to 39 show reduced penetrance; 40 or more are fully penetrant in a usual lifespan.','https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK1305/'),
('biology-L07','Median survival has risen from about 5 years in 1960 to 44 years in 2022','44.2 years is the registry median age at death for 2022, not median survival.','The ACFDR 2023 report lists 2022 median age at death 44.2 years and median survival 58.2 years for the 2017-to-2021 cohort. Keep the measures and cohort years distinct.','https://www.cysticfibrosis.org.au/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/ACFDR_2023_Annual-Report.pdf'),
('biology-L07','every Australian baby is tested for PKU and more than 25 other metabolic conditions within 48 to 72 hours of birth.','Screening is offered with consent; it is not literally performed on every baby. Program panels vary and include non-metabolic conditions.','Newborn bloodspot screening is offered to all babies, with parental consent, usually around 48 to 72 hours; name the current state program if listing its panel.','https://www.health.gov.au/sites/default/files/documents/2020/10/newborn-bloodspot-screening-national-policy-framework.pdf'),
('biology-L08','Remove the exposure and the disease does not occur.','Removal of one exposure does not remove every pathway to a disease, nor erase earlier injury.','Reducing exposure lowers the risk from that exposure; disease can still follow past exposure or other causes.','https://www.cancer.gov/about-cancer/causes-prevention/risk/substances/asbestos/asbestos-fact-sheet'),
('biology-L08',"Australia has the world's highest melanoma rate, about 15,000 new cases a year",'Undated old case count and overly definite international ranking.','AIHW estimates about 17400 melanoma diagnoses in Australia in 2025 (projection); Australia has one of the highest incidence rates. State the estimate year and source vintage.','https://www.aihw.gov.au/reports/cancer/cancer-data-in-australia/contents/cancer-data-commentaries/melanoma-of-the-skin-in-australia'),
('biology-L08','Smoking causes roughly 21,000 Australian deaths each year','The figure is an undated historical attributable estimate.','AIHW estimated smoking contributed to about 21000 Australian deaths in 2015. Keep the year and measure, or use a current dated estimate.','https://www.aihw.gov.au/getmedia/9217f50d-0d82-4112-a148-294d20d053fd/aihw-bod-20-factsheet.pdf.aspx'),
('biology-L09','found 7.5% already had Type 2 diabetes, most without knowing it.','AusDiab found roughly half, not most, of baseline diabetes was undiagnosed; the estimate must not silently become type-2-only prevalence.','The 1999-to-2000 baseline tested adults aged 25 and over and found about half of diabetes was undiagnosed. Keep the historical population and date.','https://www.aihw.gov.au/getmedia/478f1d59-bfbe-43a3-961b-a583afb41b26/aihw-cvd-96-diabetes-australian-facts-30-june-2023.pdf'),
('biology-L09','About 1.3 million Australians are diagnosed with Type 2 diabetes','The 2022 ABS figure covers diabetes overall.','The 2022 National Health Survey estimated 1.3 million Australians reported diabetes, including types other than type 2. Cite the survey definition and year.','https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/health/health-conditions-and-risks/diabetes/2022'),
('biology-L09','liver, muscle and fat cells respond by downregulating their insulin receptors. This is insulin resistance','Makes receptor downregulation the single mechanism and hides tissue-specific effects.','Muscle and adipose insulin signalling can fail to recruit GLUT4 normally; hepatic insulin resistance includes failure to suppress glucose production. Insulin resistance has multiple molecular mechanisms.',insulin),
('biology-L09','a fasting glucose above 7 mmol/L is diagnostic.','Wrong inclusion boundary and missing plasma/repeat-testing context.','Fasting plasma glucose of 7.0 mmol/L or more is one diagnostic criterion, normally confirmed by repeat testing unless unequivocal symptoms/hyperglycaemia apply.','https://www.racgp.org.au/getattachment/7c05e922-ab1f-4301-aab7-f4f9b638cb66/Management-of-type-2-diabetes-A-handbook-for-general-practice.aspx'),
('biology-L09','Vitamin D (calcitriol)','Conflates the nutrient with its active metabolite.','Vitamin D is activated to calcitriol in the body.','https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Vitamind-HealthProfessional/'),
('biology-L09',"Coronary heart disease remains Australia's leading cause of death",'The current national ranking has changed.','Dementia including Alzheimer disease was the leading cause in 2024 in the ABS release; ischaemic heart disease was second. Use the revised 2024 table if adding exact counts.',death),
]
norm=lambda s:re.sub(r'\s+',' ',s).strip()
confirmed=[]; unmatched=[]; skipped=[]
for key,old,problem,correct,source in rows:
 if norm(old) not in norm(site[key]['text']):unmatched.append({'page':key,'old':old});continue
 if old in existing:skipped.append({'page':key,'old':old});continue
 confirmed.append((key,old,problem,correct,source))
t='# Brief 117 proposed Module 8 site corrections\n\nFor root integration only. No site or shared corrections file was changed. Checked 30 October 2026 against the read-only HTML. Exact text extraction and original file SHA-256 hashes: `brief117-site-evidence.json`. Tags and repeated whitespace are omitted. Existing log checked before proposing each row.\n\n'
t+='| Lesson and page | Exact page text | Problem | Correct statement | Source |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n'
for key,old,problem,correct,source in confirmed:
 p=site[key]['path'].split('/subjects/')[-1]
 citation=f'[source]({source})' if source.startswith('https:') else source
 t+=f'| {key}, `{p}` | "{old}" | {problem} | {correct} | {citation} |\n'
t+='\n## Method and source notes, not clear factual-error additions\n\n'
t+='- L04 origin: an ideal analyte-only Beer-Lambert line is through zero after suitable blank correction. Real calibration intercepts need checking. The page\'s conditional "If Beer-Lambert holds" is not by itself false; qualify the worked instruction rather than logging all ideal-origin wording as wrong.\n'
t+='- L04 Flint: the 397 micrograms/L residence reading is documented, but the exact analytical method and "triggered federal action" attribution were not established. Virginia Tech/EPA\'s later study used ICP-MS. Do not claim that every Flint sample was ICP-MS or that AAS was essential for this particular result. [Published study](https://vtechworks.lib.vt.edu/items/15a3581f-884a-4dc5-8b86-90f2794a3790).\n'
t+='- L03 safety: add a lead hazard wherever lead results are discussed, but follow the settled rule: student unknowns contain no lead. Do not copy the design\'s teacher-dispensed student-lead recommendation into the site log. Product SDS review remains incomplete.\n'
t+='- L05: the capillary\'s bore and shoot determine mm/min, so "typical" speeds cannot be universal. A practical setup and equal-area repeated stomatal counts are coverage improvements. Wind thins the humid boundary layer; it cannot guarantee a maximum gradient regardless of humidity and temperature.\n'
t+='- L06 89% and the 1940-to-1990 transition period: a reproducible ABS/AIHW calculation was not found. Remove or source these exact denominators and years; they are unsupported here, not independently proved numerically false.\n'
t+='- L06 WHO figures are historical, not current. The WHO fact sheet updated 25 September 2025 gives at least 43 million NCD deaths in 2021, about 75% of non-pandemic deaths. Preserve that denominator; do not substitute 75% of all deaths. [WHO](https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/noncommunicable-diseases).\n'
t+='- L06 BRAF is a growth-signalling gene and CDKN2A a division-control tumour suppressor. Their inclusion under genes controlling cell division is not a clear error. Do not assert that every BRAF mutation is a direct UV-signature mutation.\n'
t+='- L07 3500 people is an older rounded count. The ACFDR 2023 report gives 3738 registry participants in 2022, 3798 in 2023. These are registry counts, not automatically complete prevalence. Current birth incidence and the 1960 survival estimate remain unverified.\n'
t+='- L08 BRAF "about 60%": not a confirmed error. The NCBI medical-genetics chapter reports approximately 50 to 60%; estimates depend on subtype. [NCBI](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK447416/).\n'
t+='- L08 latency 20-to-40 versus 20-to-50 years is a consistency repair, not proof one typical range is false. Cancer Australia supports 20 to 50; ASSEA also uses 20 to 60. Use "often decades" or a sourced typical range, not a hard limit.\n'
t+='- L08 smoking/asbestos multiplier: reject a universal 50-to-90-fold rule; retain a sourced historical cohort if explicitly identified. NCI supports a more-than-additive interaction for lung cancer, not mesothelioma. [NCI](https://www.cancer.gov/about-cancer/causes-prevention/risk/substances/asbestos/asbestos-fact-sheet).\n'
t+='- L08 IARC-2020/22-cancer attribution remains unverified. Do not turn an unlocated attribution into a false numerical certainty. Commercial solaria were banned nationwide by 2016, not uniformly since 2015; private beds can still exist. [ARPANSA](https://www.arpansa.gov.au/understanding-radiation/radiation-sources/more-radiation-sources/solaria).\n'
t+='- L09 500000 undiagnosed, current re-emergent iodine deficiency, and "the leading cause" of each diabetes complication need their own dated sources. No unsupported replacement figures are proposed. The 2009 bread rule addresses pre-existing iodine deficiency; organic bread and home bread mixes are exceptions. Vitamin-D deficiency causes osteomalacia in adults and can contribute to osteoporosis, which is not synonymous with osteomalacia.\n'
t+='- L07 Winkler: keep MnO(OH)2 as a method note for c06, not a new G02 teaching segment. The hydrated operational precipitate is not necessarily one pure compound; MnO2 shorthand does not change the oxygen/thiosulfate stoichiometry. [NOAA](https://www.nodc.noaa.gov/archive/arc0001/9900162/2.2/data/0-data/jgofscd/Files/protocols/chap6.html).\n'
t+=f'\nConfirmed proposed rows: {len(confirmed)}. Exact-text matches already in the shared log: {len(skipped)}. Candidate exact excerpts not found: {len(unmatched)}; see `brief117-site-log-audit.json`. These were not silently added.\n'
if chr(8212) in t:raise ValueError('em dash')
(A/'brief117-site-corrections-proposed.md').write_text(t,encoding='utf-8')
(A/'brief117-site-log-audit.json').write_text(json.dumps({'confirmed':len(confirmed),'skipped_existing':skipped,'unmatched':unmatched},ensure_ascii=False,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
print(len(confirmed),'confirmed;',unmatched)
